# 低频词汇 List06
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025恋练有词
# 描述: 低频词汇List06核心词汇

errand /ˈerənd/ n. 差事 She ran several errands in the morning. 她早上跑了几个差事。
espionage /ˈespiənɑːːʒ/ n. 间谍活动 He was charged with industrial espionage. 他被指控从事工业间谍活动。
esteem /ɪˈstiːm/ n./v. 尊重 She is held in high esteem by her colleagues. 她受到同事们的高度尊重。
evacuate /ɪˈvækjueɪt/ v. 疏散 Residents were evacuated before the flood. 洪水来临前居民被疏散。
evoke /ɪˈvəʊk/ v. 唤起 The painting evokes a sense of nostalgia. 这幅画唤起了一种怀旧感。
excerpt /ˈeksɜːpt/ n./v. 摘录 The article included an excerpt from the speech. 文章包括了演讲的一段摘录。
exempt /ɪɡˈzempt/ v./adj. 免除 Students with high scores are exempt from the exam. 高分学生免考。
exile /ˈeksaɪl/ n./v. 流放 The political leader was sent into exile. 这位政治领导人被流放。
exotic /ɪɡˈzɒtɪk/ adj. 异国的 The market sells exotic fruits from around the world. 这个市场销售来自世界各地的异国水果。
expenditure /ɪkˈspendɪtʃə(r)/ n. 开支 Government expenditure on education has increased. 政府的教育开支增加了。
expire /ɪkˈspaɪə(r)/ v. 到期 The contract expires at the end of the year. 合同年底到期。
explicit /ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/ adj. 明确的 The law has explicit requirements for safety. 法律对安全有明确的要求。
extinct /ɪkˈstɪŋkt/ adj. 灭绝的 Many species have become extinct. 许多物种已经灭绝。
extract /ɪkˈstrækt/ v./n. 提取 Oil is extracted from underground reserves. 石油从地下储量中提取。
fabricate /ˈfæbrɪkeɪt/ v. 制造；捏造 The witness was accused of fabricating evidence. 证人被指控捏造证据。
faction /ˈfækʃn/ n. 派系 The party is divided into several factions. 该党分裂成几个派系。
feat /fiːt/ n. 壮举 Building the bridge was an engineering feat. 建造这座桥是一项工程壮举。
fervent /ˈfɜːvənt/ adj. 热烈的 She is a fervent supporter of environmental causes. 她是环保事业的热心支持者。
fiscal /ˈfɪskl/ adj. 财政的 The government announced new fiscal measures. 政府宣布了新的财政措施。
flaw /flɔː/ n. 缺陷 The plan has a fundamental flaw. 这个计划有一个根本性的缺陷。
flee /fliː/ v. 逃离 Thousands fled the war-torn country. 数千人逃离了这个饱受战争蹂躏的国家。
fluctuate /ˈflʌktʃueɪt/ v. 波动 Prices fluctuate with market conditions. 价格随市场条件波动。
forge /fɔːdʒ/ v. 锻造；伪造 The two nations forged a strong alliance. 两国建立了牢固的联盟。
forthcoming /ˌfɔːθˈkʌmɪŋ/ adj. 即将来临的 The forthcoming conference will address these issues. 即将召开的会议将讨论这些问题。
foster /ˈfɒstə(r)/ v. 培养 The school fosters creativity in students. 学校培养学生的创造力。
franchise /ˈfræntʃaɪz/ n. 特许经营权 He bought a fast-food franchise. 他买了一个快餐特许经营权。
frantic /ˈfræntɪk/ adj. 疯狂的 There was a frantic search for the missing child. 人们疯狂地搜寻失踪的孩子。
fraud /frɔːd/ n. 欺诈 He was convicted of financial fraud. 他被判犯有金融欺诈罪。
fringe /frɪndʒ/ n./adj. 边缘 The idea was once considered fringe. 这个想法曾被认为是边缘的。
futile /ˈfjuːtaɪl/ adj. 徒劳的 All attempts to save the building were futile. 挽救这座建筑的所有尝试都是徒劳的。
